  "worked_solution": "The inequality $x<5$ corresponds to all numbers less than $5.$ A number line for this interval is shown below:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191214/assets/61a3fcdcc19f822c0d94b806441ea2888dab3bb9ac0b846c965a8fe23ad078ae.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the segment on the number line, we have the following:\n\n- There is no left endpoint - it continues forever. So, we write the interval with negative infinity as the left endpoint, not included.\n\n- The right endpoint $5$ is *not* included in the interval.\n\nTherefore, using interval notation, we represent $x<5$ as\n\n$$\nx\\in (-\\infty ,5).\n$$",
